"""Schema spec for the Genpact F&A master-data tables.

Single source of truth for three consumers so they cannot drift:

* ``app/models/genpact_master_data.py`` — builds SQLAlchemy Core ``Table``
  objects on ``Base.metadata`` from this spec (so Alembic autogenerate
  sees them and the ORM ``Base`` can create them).
* the Alembic migration that creates the tables (autogenerated from the
  metadata above).
* ``scripts/seed_genpact_master_data.py`` — reads the workbook and bulk
  inserts rows, applying the per-column coercion declared here.

The source workbook (``Genpact_FA_Synthetic_Employee_Dataset.xlsx``) has
many sheets. The clearly-structured ones each become one table, scoped
to a single tenant via a ``tenant_id`` column. Columns are mapped
**positionally** (spec order == sheet column order) because several
sheet headers contain trailing spaces / typos that make name matching
fragile. ``header_row`` is the 0-based row that holds the headers; data
starts on the row after it.

A column spec is ``(attr, kind, length_or_precision)``:

* ``kind`` is one of ``str | text | int | bigint | num | date | bool``.
* for ``str`` the 3rd item is the ``String`` length.
* for ``num`` the 3rd item is the ``(precision, scale)`` tuple.
* otherwise the 3rd item is ``None``.

Blank cells are coerced to a type default (never NULL) so downstream
consumers can rely on non-null business columns.
"""

